// expect: 42
// BANKED RED (unregistered — Hβ.synth.fan-extraction-needs-a-feeder).
// The fork/merge composition's FIRING case, written before it can fire.
//
// verify_each_enriched runs both halves in the forced order today: the
// fan proves meaning by forking, then saturate_range + egraph_extract
// pick the cheapest FORM of each survivor, and survivors sharing an
// e-class collapse to one proposal. That path is live and
// non-destructive. What it cannot yet DO is move anything, and the
// reason is structural, not a bug: the e-graph's rules all match
// BinOpExpr shapes (rw_add_identity / rw_mul_identity / rw_mul_absorb /
// rw_sub_identity / rw_div_identity / rw_const_fold, egraph.mn:123-224)
// while every fan enumerator mints an ATOM — an int/float/string
// literal, a unit, a ctor call, a lambda, a record, a list, a tuple
// (synth_proposer.mn:684-693 and kin). The two sets do not intersect,
// so extraction always chases a handle to itself.
//
// This fixture is what firing looks like: a hole whose proven candidate
// has a strictly cheaper equivalent, so extraction moves it and the
// proposal the developer sees is the reduced form. It runs green the
// day a FEEDER exists — either a candidate space that mints composite
// expressions, or a rule set that rewrites the shapes the fan already
// mints (band G's saturation-deepen). Until then it stands as the
// artifact that says what "fed" means.
fn scale(x) = x * 1

fn main() = {
  let v = scale(42)
  if v == 42 { 42 } else { 1 }
}
